    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this superb three-bedroom end-of-terrace family home to the Finglas property market, ideally positioned on the ever-popular Casement Road. Set on a large site and benefiting from a generous front driveway, side garage and substantial rear patio garden, No. 455 offers excellent proportions both internally and externally together with fantastic potential to further modernise and add value.\n\nInternal accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch leading into a welcoming hallway, a bright living room located just off the hallway, and a large kitchen/dining room to the rear. The kitchen provides access into a rear extension, which in turn opens out onto the large rear patio garden. Upstairs there are two generous double bedrooms, both benefiting from built-in wardrobes, a single bedroom and a family bathroom.\n\nNo. 455 Casement Road extends to approximately c. 86 sq.m and offers bright, spacious and well-proportioned accommodation throughout. The property has been well maintained and provides a practical layout with excellent scope for a new owner to modernise and put their own stamp on the home. Additional benefits include gas-fired central heating, double glazed windows throughout, a large front driveway providing ample off-street parking and a side garage benefiting from electricity.\n\nCasement Road is within easy reach of Finglas Village and Charlestown Shopping Centre, offering an excellent selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, sports clubs and recreational facilities. DCU, IKEA, Clearwater Shopping Centre and The National Botanic Gardens are also all within easy reach. The area is exceptionally well connected, with numerous Dublin Bus routes serving the surrounding area and providing frequent access to Dublin City Centre and beyond. The M50, N2, N3, M1 and Dublin Airport are all easily accessible, making this an ideal location for commuters.\n\nViewing is highly recommended. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today on 0861985247 or 015411455 to arrange a viewing or for further information.\n\nAdditional Features:\n• BER E\n• c. 86 sq.m\n• Built 1963\n• Three-bedroom end-of-terrace family home\n• Family bathroom\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Double glazed windows throughout\n• Large front driveway with ample off-street parking\n• Side garage with electricity\n• Entrance porch\n• Welcoming entrance hallway\n• Bright living room\n• Large kitchen/dining room\n• Rear extension\n• Two generous double bedrooms with built-in wardrobes\n• Spacious single bedroom\n• Family bathroom\n• Large rear patio garden\n• Gated side access\n• Large site\n• Excellent potential to modernise and add value\n• Mature and highly sought-after residential location\n• Close to Finglas Village and Charlestown Shopping Centre\n• Excellent selection of local schools and amenities\n• Easy access to the M50, N2, N3, M1 and Dublin Airport\n• Well serviced by public transport"
      },
